{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1001", "sample_idx": 6, "model_name": "stockmark/stockmark-2-100b-instruct", "content": "To Japan doth thou journey, and I, thy faithful scribe, shall weave the tale of thy adventure in a style befitting the bard himself.\n\nFirst, in Tokyo, where the neon lights doth dance upon the night, thy feet shall tread the grounds of the Imperial Palace, where the history of the Samurai and the Shogun doth lie. Then, at the Meiji Shrine, thou shalt find peace amidst the bustling city, where the ancient traditions are preserved in the heart of modernity.\n\nNext, in Kyoto, the former capital, where the culture and beauty doth flourish, thou shalt visit the Kinkaku-ji, the Golden Pavilion, where the reflection of the sun doth turn the waters into gold. And at the Arashiyama Bamboo Grove, thou shalt walk amidst the towering green, as if in a fairytale, where the wind doth whisper through the canes, and the soul doth find solace.\n\nAt Nara, where the deer roam free, thou shalt visit Todai-ji, where the Great Buddha doth stand with a serene smile, and the echoes of the past doth resonate in the halls.\n\nLastly, in Hiroshima, thou shalt visit the Peace Memorial Park, where the memories of the past doth serve as a reminder of the importance of peace, and the Children's Peace Monument doth stand as a testament to the resilience of the human spirit.\n\nThus, thy journey through Japan shall be a tale of history, culture, and the enduring spirit of a people, as told by the pen of a scribe inspired by the words of the great bard.", "logprobs": [{"token": "To", "logprob": -2.2972445487976074}, {"token": " Japan", "logprob": -1.1780287027359009}, {"token": " d", "logprob": -2.5344996452331543}, {"token": "oth", "logprob": -0.38790205121040344}, {"token": " thou", "logprob": -0.4629770517349243}, {"token": " journey", "logprob": -1.515251874923706}, {"token": ",", "logprob": -0.33271893858909607}, {"token": " and", "logprob": -1.6316685676574707}, {"to